## 1. Modular Directory & Package Layout

Enterprise iOS applications organize code by **feature vertical slices**, strictly enforcing layer isolation. Code must never be organized into generic monolithic folders.

```text
EnterpriseApp/
├── Core/                                   # Shared enterprise infrastructure
│   ├── Network/                            # URLSession client, interceptors & SSL pinning
│   ├── Security/                           # Keychain hardware vault & Secure Enclave auth
│   ├── Persistence/                        # SwiftData ModelContainer & schema migrations
│   └── UI/Theme/                           # Enterprise design tokens (Colors, Typography, Spacing)
│
├── DI/                                     # Global singleton dependency injection
│   └── AppContainer.swift                  # Root container wiring shared infrastructure
│
└── Features/User/                          # USER FEATURE MODULE (Vertical Slice)
    ├── Data/                               # Data Layer: Single Source of Truth
    │   ├── Remote/
    │   │   ├── DTO/UserNetworkDTO.swift    # Codable API serialization model
    │   │   └── UserEndpoint.swift          # URLRequest builder & HTTP endpoint contract
    │   ├── Local/
    │   │   ├── Model/UserPersistentModel.swift # SwiftData @Model schema
    │   │   └── Storage/UserLocalStore.swift    # SwiftData Actor / query operations
    │   ├── Mapper/UserMappers.swift        # Bidirectional DTO <-> Persistent <-> Domain mappers
    │   └── Repository/UserRepositoryImpl.swift # Repository implementation (Cache + Network)
    │
    ├── Domain/                             # Pure Domain Layer: Zero UIKit / SwiftUI APIs
    │   ├── Model/UserDomainModel.swift     # Sendable immutable Swift business model
    │   ├── Repository/UserRepository.swift # Protocol boundary contract
    │   └── UseCase/GetUserProfileUseCase.swift # Single-purpose business use case
    │
    ├── DI/                                 # Feature-scoped Dependency Injection
    │   └── UserFeatureContainer.swift      # Resolves repository interfaces to implementations
    │
    └── Presentation/                       # UI Layer: SwiftUI + @Observable ViewModels
        ├── State/
        │   ├── UserProfileUIState.swift    # Value-type enum representing screen states
        │   └── UserProfileUIIntent.swift   # User actions & screen interaction intents
        ├── ViewModel/
        │   └── UserProfileViewModel.swift  # @Observable @MainActor ViewModel
        └── Views/
            ├── UserProfileView.swift       # Stateless Screen Composable with Navigation
            └── Components/ProfileHeaderView.swift # Reusable atomic SwiftUI components
```

