## 5. Architectural Anti-Patterns & Prohibitions

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">CRITICAL IOS VIOLATIONS</div>
  <p>Pull Requests containing any of the following anti-patterns will be automatically blocked by Danger CI:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Retain Cycles in Closures:</strong> Never capture <code>self</code> strongly in asynchronous Tasks or network completion handlers. Always use <code>[weak self]</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Mutating UI Outside @MainActor:</strong> ViewModels and state publishers must be explicitly marked <code>@MainActor</code> to prevent background-thread UI mutations.</li>
    <li><strong>Legacy ObservableObject in iOS 17+:</strong> Do not use deprecated <code>ObservableObject</code> and <code>@Published</code> for new code. All ViewModels must use the Swift 5.9+ <code>@Observable</code> macro.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct SwiftData Queries in Views:</strong> Views must never query <code>ModelContext</code> or perform database fetch descriptors directly. All data access must pass through a Use Case and ViewModel.</li>
    <li><strong>Force Unwrapping:</strong> Force unwrapping with <code>!</code> or <code>try!</code> is strictly prohibited in production code and will fail linting gates.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

