## 5. Architectural Anti-Patterns & Prohibitions

<div class="portal-alert-box">
  <div class="portal-alert-title">CRITICAL REACT NATIVE VIOLATIONS</div>
  <p>Pull Requests containing any of the following anti-patterns will be automatically blocked by Danger CI:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Unencrypted AsyncStorage for Sensitive Tokens:</strong> Never store authentication tokens, session secrets, or PII in standard <code>AsyncStorage</code>. Always use <code>@enterprise/react-native-auth</code> backed by hardware KeyStore / Keychain.</li>
    <li><strong>Inline Function Allocations in List Render Items:</strong> Passing arrow functions or non-memoized objects to <code>renderItem</code> inside <code>FlashList</code> or <code>FlatList</code> causes bridge flooding and severe dropped frames. Always use <code>useCallback</code> and <code>useMemo</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Bypassing Clean Architecture Layers:</strong> Components must never query Axios or MMKV directly. All reads and writes must pass through a custom hook and use case.</li>
    <li><strong>Direct State Mutation:</strong> Mutating Zustand or React state objects directly bypasses equality checks and breaks Unidirectional Data Flow. Always return fresh immutable objects.</li>
    <li><strong>Catching and Swallowing Errors Silently:</strong> Silent <code>catch &#123;&#125;</code> blocks prevent distributed network traces from reporting failures to Datadog RUM. Always log or propagate unhandled errors.</li>
  </ul>
